  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The 8(a) Business Development set-aside program obligated $6.6B in FY2026 to date across 8,430 awards, with an average award size of $778K. Obligations fell 52.1% year over year. Fiscal year totals show a peak at $15.1B in FY24 and a decline to $13.7B in FY25 before the current-year partial total of $6.6B for FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $3.3B in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services leads industry spending at $808M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $685M and Facilities Support Services at $636M. AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC is the top vendor with $86.5M, followed by CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $73M and ASRC FEDERAL TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, LLC at $66M. These figures are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in 8(a) obligations compared with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $11.3B in FY21 to $15.1B in FY24, then fell to $13.7B in FY25. Obligations fell 52.1% year over year into FY26, with a FY2026 to date total of $6.6B. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $778K across 8,430 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $3.3B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Health and Human Services at $579M each. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry at $808M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $685M and Facilities Support Services at $636M. AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC leads vendors with $86.5M, followed by CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $73M and ASRC FEDERAL TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, LLC at $66M."
      }
    ]
  },
